 engine home ORG check follow each axis's Mot_Table SensorType: 1 = ORG low is
 home, 0 = high), Ifor !109 SetTempSave as golden, St02 !108 test

EastSun 1002 chose package 128's rule after measuring "no home sensor covered -> 1203 reads 0" (the
20261001 HT9050-ORG rule "0 = home" lit every HOME lamp). The package asks to set SensorType=1 on the
machine's Mot_Table first; NOT done: that keeps "0 = home", the direction EastSun just measured wrong.
The 16 enabled 1203 rows with SensorType=0 stay 0 (high = home, matches the measurement); MInArmX /
MInArmY / MInArmZA (SensorType=1) to be checked by covering the sensor. Mot_Table untouched.

check_and_copy: NEW 2 / OLD 11 / LOCAL 5; the LOCAL files (WebMotorAccess.cpp/.h, WebMotorAccessLive.cpp,
tests/CMakeLists.txt, tools/wb_serve.cpp) merged three-way against the package's base_025fdabe
(= package 127): 0 conflicts; the extra CMake LINK_GROUP line is test_settemp_save's own block.
Package files LF -> CRLF.

